## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs’ Mercury Edit 2 is a diffusion-based next-edit prediction model for code autocomplete (FIM) and multi-line edits, specialized for low-latency editor workflows.
- **Provider / access:** Inception Labs API. Local metadata lists `inception/mercury-edit-2`, pricing $0.25/$0.75 per 1M ($0.025 cached), and 32K context.
- **Release / knowledge:** Inception Labs docs reviewed 2026-11-10. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed source.
- **IDs:** `mercury-edit-2`, `inception/mercury-edit-2`.
- **Context window:** 32,000 tokens total; 8,192 max output.
- **Modalities:** Text input; text output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $0.25/$0.75 per 1M in/out ($0.025 cached) per metadata/docs.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary diffusion-based code editing model (closed weights). Architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SELF-EXCLUSION: Mercury Edit 2 is a specialized FIM/next-edit endpoint model rather than a general conversational/chat benchmark target. Inception Labs docs reviewed via `webfetch` provide API usage/specs and pricing but no independently verifiable standardized benchmark numerics (e.g. SWE-bench, LiveCodeBench, HumanEval-style public suite results) for this exact model. To avoid unverifiable or misattributed scoring, this file is saved as `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

